From 90fed73dfd6cf0f5e53f92998a43b2825f5ab94d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleg Tolmatcev <oleg.tolmatcev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 00:39:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pwd, realpath, readlink: print paths with / on Windows

The shell's pwd prints C:/src/build, uutils' pwd printed C:\src\build.
Scripts read printed paths as POSIX shell or Tcl words, where \s and
\b are escapes: gcc's Makefile writes $(shell pwd), which make runs
without a shell, into its testsuite's site.exp, and every c-torture
"builtins" test linked to "C:srcuild-gccgcc/...".  pwd, realpath and
readlink now print / separators on Windows (uucore::fs::
posix_separators); Windows accepts both.  The tests expect / there.
